      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is double the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. The usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg/day total.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day. This is a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the absolute ceiling and is rarely needed.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter the order once you do."
      }
     ],
