     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The total is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) justifies a dose that high. Ibuprofen has a ceiling effect for pain and inflammation, so the extra drug adds GI bleeding, kidney, and cardiovascular risk without adding benefit.\n\nYou have two ways to move forward:\n1. **Change the dose.** Tell me which regimen you want, such as 400 mg four times daily, 600 mg four times daily, or 800 mg three times daily. I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Get attending sign-off.** If your attending or resident really wants this dose, they should enter it themselves or tell you the clinical reason. They can also talk to pharmacy about it. I can add a note to the order if you want one.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
